Three small fixes to xml2abc.py version 177 (Wim Vree, LGPL), applied by setup.sh.
This is the xml2abc the Part 2 reward used. Apply from the folder holding xml2abc.py:
    patch -p1 < xml2abc-177.patch

Each hunk touches only code that used to raise an exception, so any file that converted before still takes
exactly the same path through the code. Checked on Part 1's 1,443 canonical keyboard pieces: ABC byte-identical
and score identical for all 1,443.

1. Additive meters (doAttr). <beats>2+2+3</beats> crashed int(beats). Now it writes M:(2+2+3)/8 (header or
   inline [M:...]) and sets the internal meter to the sum (7/8). abc2midi 5.04 accepts this form (in our test, the
   MIDI was byte-identical to the same piece written as M:7/8). Integer meters are unchanged.
2. Pedal change (doDirection). <pedal type="change"/> raised ValueError('wrong direction type'). Now it writes
   !ped-up!!ped! (lift and re-press) at that point and leaves the pedal down. Other unknown direction types still
   raise. (Pedal is MIDI CC64, which the MiMo scorer ignores.)
3. Overfull 5/8 and 7/8 bars (bpltel). A note starting at or after the 7th eighth indexed past the end of a
   7-element list (IndexError). The index is now clamped to 6. The value only matters with --rbm, which this
   route never passes, so this changes output only for files that crashed before.

Why: the model writes these three things (additive meters, pedal changes, occasionally an overfull bar), and the
unpatched converter crashed on them, which would have excluded those pieces from training instead of scoring them.
The run's copy differs from the result of this patch only in the wording of the three "# PATCH" comments.

--- a/xml2abc.py
+++ b/xml2abc.py
@@ -631,7 +631,7 @@
     tel = int (nx.tijd // noemer)   # == floor ()
     if metrum [1] == 8:
         if metrum [0] == 7 or metrum [0] == 5:
-            tel = [0,0,0,1,1,2,2][tel]
+            tel = [0,0,0,1,1,2,2][min (tel, 6)]  # PATCH (Part 2): overfull 5/8 or 7/8 bar (onset >= 7 eighths); tel only matters with --rbm
         else:
             tel = int (tel // 3)
     return tel, noemer
@@ -1293,9 +1293,13 @@
         if beats:
             unit = e.findtext ('time/beat-type')
             mtr = beats + '/' + unit
+            if '+' in beats:    # PATCH (Part 2): additive meter (e.g. 2+2+3) -> M:(2+2+3)/8, numerator = sum
+                mtr = '(%s)/%s' % ('+'.join (b.strip () for b in beats.split ('+')), unit)
+                nbeats = sum (int (b) for b in beats.split ('+'))
+            else: nbeats = int (beats)
             if first: abcOut.mtr = mtr          # first measure -> header
             else: s.msr.attr += '[M:%s]' % mtr  # otherwise -> voice
-            s.msr.mtr = int (beats), int (unit)
+            s.msr.mtr = nbeats, int (unit)
         s.msr.mdur = (s.msr.divs * s.msr.mtr[0] * 4) // s.msr.mtr[1]   # duration of measure in xml-divisions
         for ms in e.findall('measure-style'):
             n = int (ms.get ('number', '1'))    # staff number
@@ -1400,6 +1404,9 @@
                 else:                               # closing direction found before opening
                     s.dirStk [k] = ('stop', s.msc.tijd)
                     x = ''                          # delay code generation until opening found
+            elif type == 'change' and dtype == 'pedal': # PATCH (Part 2): pedal change = lift + re-press at this point
+                x = '!ped-up!!ped!'
+                if k not in s.dirStk: s.dirStk [k] = (('start', vs))  # pedal is down after the change
             else: raise ValueError ('wrong direction type')
             addDirection (x, vs, None, stfnum)
         tempo, wrdstxt = None, ''
